    'Kibale Forest National Park in western Uganda is widely regarded as the best chimpanzee trekking destination in the world. The park\'s 766 km² of moist tropical forest supports the highest density of primates anywhere in Africa — 13 species including over 1,500 chimpanzees, red colobus monkeys, red-tailed monkeys, L\'Hoest\'s monkeys and black-and-white colobus.',
    'The chimpanzees of Kibale are habituated to human presence and can be tracked on foot with ranger guides every morning from Kanyanchu Visitor Centre. Unlike gorilla trekking where you spend one hour with the gorillas, chimpanzee trekking at Kibale offers up to one hour of observation once found — watching the chimps feeding, grooming, socialising and travelling through the canopy.',
    'The Bigodi Wetland Sanctuary adjacent to the park is an extraordinary complement to the chimp trek — a community-run guided walk through papyrus wetland and forest that produces excellent primate and bird sightings including the sitatunga antelope, 11 primate species and over 200 bird species in a 2-hour walk.',
